{"id":"bicicleta","lemma":"bicicleta","pos":"noun","rank":1954,"glosses":["bicycle, pushbike, cycle","step over, pedalada (a dribbling move, or feint, in football (soccer), used to fool a defensive player into thinking the offensive player, in possession of the ball, is going to move in a direction he does not intend to move in)","bicycle"],"ipa":"/biθiˈkleta/","gender":"f","forms":{"plural":"bicicletas"},"audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/07/LL-Q1321_%28spa%29-AdrianAbdulBaha-bicicleta.wav","formAudio":{"bicicletas":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/aa/LL-Q1321_%28spa%29-Wikipedian-walker-bicicletas.wav"},"examples":[{"text":"Ella tiene una bicicleta.","en":"She has a bike.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/525412"},{"text":"Durante un tiempo vendí bicicletas.","en":"I sold bicycles for a while."},{"text":"Prefiero ir en bicicleta.","en":"I prefer biking.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/441661"},{"text":"Vamos a montar en las bicicletas.","en":"Let's go on our bicycles."},{"text":"Él tiene una bicicleta.","en":"He has a bicycle.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/734243"}]}